  "full_response": "Here’s a professional and polite customer complaint email template that includes all the requested details:\n\n---\n\n**Subject:** Complaint Regarding Order #[Order Number]\n\nDear [Customer Service Team/Company Name],\n\nI hope this email finds you well. I am writing to express my dissatisfaction with a recent order I placed with your company. Below are the details of my order and the issues I encountered:\n\n**Order Details:**\n- **Order Number:** [Insert Order Number]\n- **Full Name:** [Your Full Name]\n- **Email Address:** [Your Email Address]\n- **Phone Number:** [Your Phone Number]\n- **Home Address:** [Your Full Street Address, City, State, ZIP Code]\n\n**Issue Description:**\n[Clearly and concisely describe the problem. For example:\n- The item(s) arrived damaged/defective.\n- The wrong item(s) were shipped.\n- The order was incomplete or missing items.\n- The delivery was late or never arrived.\n- The product does not match the description or expectations.]\n\n**Additional Details:**\n[Provide any relevant details, such as:\n- Photos of the damaged item or packaging (attach if possible).\n- Dates of delivery or expected delivery.\n- Any previous attempts to resolve the issue (e.g., phone calls, chats).]\n\n**Requested Resolution:**\nI would appreciate it if you could [state what you’d like them to do, such as:\n- Replace the item(s) at no additional cost.\n- Issue a full or partial refund.\n- Provide a return shipping label.\n- Offer a discount on a future purchase.]\n\nI value your company’s products/services and hope this matter can be resolved promptly. Please let me know how you plan to address this issue or if you require any further information from me. I look forward to your response within [reasonable timeframe, e.g., 5 business days].\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Full Name]\n[Your Phone Number]\n[Your Email Address]\n\n---\n\n### Tips for Writing an Effective Complaint Email:\n1. **Be polite but firm** – Avoid aggressive language; focus on facts and solutions.\n2. **Keep it concise** – Stick to the key details to make it easy for the company to address.\n3. **Attach evidence** – Include photos, receipts, or screenshots if applicable.\n4. **Set a reasonable deadline** – Give them a timeframe to respond (e.g., 5–7 business days).",
